Z||000000||MooCow||09-27-2000||04:10 PM||||Okay I just installed my heater core and now my car will not start??  Could it be I don't have enough antifreeze cause a bunch unloaded when i took out the heater core and I mean a bunch all over the inside of the car.  Someone help me quick so I can insurance on it today and drive it to see if it works.   PLEASE HELP<P>                          Thanks Ken||||reg||11
Z||000001||HugGRRRFiero||09-27-2000||04:27 PM||||Not having enough antifreeze won't cause a car to not start, it will cause it to stop if you drive it too far.<P>Has this Fiero been sitting for awhile?  Could be dead battery at least that would be the first thing I'd check.<P>------------------<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">        <BR>        <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000002||MooCow||09-27-2000||04:34 PM||||Well the car started just before I even put the other heater core in and it did. Now after it is installed nothing??<P>Anyone know what the problem is at all??<BR>Please help?<P>                            Thanks Ken||||reg||5
Z||000003||HugGRRRFiero||09-27-2000||04:40 PM||||Hmmm.. if you had the passenger door open and the hood open for a long time you could have drained the battery by the interior or trunk lights.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fformula88||09-27-2000||05:16 PM||||I was just thinking what HugGRRR posted.  Sounds like the battery must have died on you from having the door open.  Mine has 4 interior bulbs that go on with the door open, plus the hood and trunk when they are open.  I have often drained the battery by leaving it all open for a day workin on it.  <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/Motorcity/Boulevard/9278/fierosig1.jpg">  <BR>1988 Fiero Formula||||reg||1
Z||000005||Steven||09-27-2000||05:28 PM||||Not to mention if you had left the ignition on or listend to the radio as you worked.||||reg||11
Z||000006||2xsess||09-27-2000||05:51 PM||||Sounds like everyone is one the same track here. Does the car even turn over? <P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||5
Z||000007||DjKid||09-27-2000||05:59 PM||||Let me get on a differant track then!<P>Perhaps the car didn't like you messing with its innards.. hehe.. and dont want to be with you anymore. The easiest fix to this is to rent a trailer and bring it to me.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>Ray - Blue 88 Coupe<BR><A HREF="http://blueknight.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank>My Blue Knight</A> - <A HREF="http://www.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank> Carolina Fieros</A>||||reg||1
Z||000008||MooCow||09-27-2000||09:17 PM||||All I had to do was jump start it like 3 times because I guess I never let the battery recharg after it jumped.  All I did was jump start it then turn it off and then relized it wouldn't jump start but now it works Great and boy did I miss it.<BR>Thanks everyone<P><BR>                            Ken||||reg||10
